after winning her multi-million dollar  lawsuit against los angeles county  vanessa bryant is paying it forward kobe  bryant's widow won 16 million dollars in  damages in court it's what a jury said  she deserved for the emotional distress  caused by leaked photos taken from the  scene of her late husband and daughter  gianna's fatal 2020 helicopter crash  we love and miss you boo boo and gigi  so where will the winnings go to a cause  near and dear to the bryant family the  los angeles times reports vanessa plans  to donate funds to the mamba and  mambasita sports foundation a non-profit  that carries on kobe and gianna's  legacies by offering opportunities to  underprivileged young athletes truly  it's a gift  it really is a gift the bryant family  wasn't the only winner in this case the  jury awarded co-plaintiff christopher  chester with 15 million dollars in  damages too he lost his wife sarah and  13 year old daughter payton in the same  crash  just moments after leaving the court  vanessa shared this instagram post in  honor of the victory quote all for you i  love you justice for kobe and gigi and  in a twist of fate the day of the big  win was kobe bryant day aka mamba day 8  24 in honor of his number 8 and number  24 lakers jerseys kobe's former teammate  shaq praised vanessa for standing strong  during the trial telling et he can't  imagine what she's going through  we live in a world where  especially when he hits the internet  people don't care but  those aren't pictures that i would ever  ever want to see so  she's doing a great thing for you know  holding the people responsible  for what they did so how did these  photos get into the wrong hands well  legal expert julie rendellman tells e.t  it's not unusual for photos to be taken  on a crime scene i think the more  significant aspect of it is not as much  whether or not they were  supposed to take those photos but the  mere fact that anyone else would have  seen them is the big problem regardless  of whether or not they were legitimately  taking those photos in the first place  she also goes into detail of why  fighting this case was so important for  vanessa first of all the county  wants the jury to believe that the  reason these photos were taken was  because they were required to be taken  and so the question becomes well were  they really required to zoom up close  uh to the remains of each of the  individuals including kobe bryant and  his child the second reason is the more  gruesome these photos are  the more emotionally distressing it is  to vanessa bryant and her family to know  that individuals that have absolutely  nothing to do and no right to view these  photos had an opportunity to do so
 

